---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

// Selected publications are drawn from the publications collection — /research holds the full record.
const AWARDS = [
  { year: '2025', name: 'Interpretation Australia Award', detail: 'Birds of Australia, STORYBOX with the Australian Museum' },
  { year: '2025', name: 'Media Architecture Biennale Award', detail: 'STORYBOX' },
  { year: '2023', name: 'NSW Heritage Award', detail: 'Building Bridges' },
  { year: '2021', name: 'Digital Placemaking Award, Commendation', detail: 'STORYBOX, Asia Pacific Place Leaders Awards' },
  { year: '2020', name: 'Smart Cities Future of Place, Finalist', detail: 'Australia and NZ Smart Cities Council Awards' },
  { year: '2016', name: 'Digital Interpretation Award, Winner', detail: 'A Keeping Place, Blacktown Native Institute. Museums and Galleries Australia' },
  { year: '2015', name: 'Outstanding Heritage Award, Winner', detail: "Mt Stromlo Director's Residence. National Trust ACT" },
  { year: '2008', name: 'Best Cross-Platform Content, Winner', detail: 'Sydney Sidetracks, ABC' },
];

const FELLOWSHIPS = [
  { year: '2023–2027', name: "Vice Chancellor's Senior Research Fellowship", detail: 'RMIT University' },
  { year: '2017', name: 'Museum of Arts and Science Research Fellowship', detail: '' },
  { year: '2015', name: 'Fellowship', detail: 'NYU Centre for Urban Science and Progress' },
  { year: '2014–2017', name: 'Postdoctoral Research Fellowship', detail: 'Urban Studies Foundation' },
  { year: '2006', name: 'Centre for Archival and Scholarly Research Fellowship', detail: 'National Film and Sound Archive' },
  { year: '2005–2009', name: 'Australian Postgraduate Award', detail: '' },
];

const selectedPubs = (await getCollection('work'))
  .filter(p => !p.data.draft && p.data.featured)
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.year - a.data.year || a.data.title.localeCompare(b.data.title));
---

<Base
  title="About — Sarah Barns"
  banner={{
    src: 'https://pub-9840de99aef84197989ef35cf41fa967.r2.dev/docklands/docklands-water.mp4',
    captionTitle: 'Docklands Waterscape',
    captionBody: 'Wurundjuri lands, Naarm/Melbourne.',
  }}
>
  <div class="page-header about-header">
    <p class="about-kicker"><span class="about-tick"></span><em>the longer story</em></p>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">Public historian and creative producer working with digital methods to enliven storied-connections between people, places, and habitats.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>For over twenty years, my work has been guided by a single question: <strong>who gets to decide what value technological systems create?</strong></p>

    <p>I came to this question through sound. My PhD examined real-time city technologies reimagined as connection points to the "real times of space" — using ambient sound archives to create mobile listening experiences that reveal contested spatial histories. That early work in experimental public history and speculative archival practice set the coordinates for everything that followed.</p>

    <p>In 2019, I published <em>Platform Urbanism: Negotiating Platform Ecosystems in Connected Cities</em> with Palgrave Macmillan. The book examines how digital platforms restructure urban life, public services, and civic participation — and asks what alternative platform models might look like when designed for public value rather than private extraction. It has been cited over 500 times.</p>

    <p>The research has since moved from platforms to AI. I currently hold a <strong>Vice Chancellor's Senior Research Fellowship</strong> at RMIT University, focused on civic AI governance — tracing the arc from platform urbanism to place-based approaches to AI sovereignty. The fellowship asks how Indigenous data sovereignty, embodied knowledge, and community participation can reshape AI governance frameworks at the local, national, and international scale.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Studio ESEM &amp; STORYBOX</h2>

    <p>Through <a href="https://studioesem.com">Studio ESEM</a> (founded 2011), I work with cultural institutions, councils, and communities to build participatory digital infrastructure. The studio sits at the intersection of research, strategy, and making — every project is both a practical intervention and a research contribution.</p>

    <p>The studio's signature project is <a href="https://storybox.co">STORYBOX</a> — a civic digital storytelling platform that deploys outdoor exhibition infrastructure for community voice. Since 2020, STORYBOX has been used by partners including ABC, the Australian Museum, the National Gallery of Australia, UNSW, and Canterbury Bankstown Council, building on over 40 placemaking programs delivered since 2013.</p>

    <p>I also publish <a href="https://civicinterplay.io">Civic Interplay</a>, a research publication exploring the intersections of civic technology, AI governance, and participatory democracy.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>The longer thread</h2>

    <p>Across all of this work — the scholarship, the studio practice, the writing — runs what I think of as a long-form narrative inquiry into how digital systems reshape place, citizenship, and collective governance. I have described this elsewhere as "golden threads structuring space through time," resisting what I call the actuarial colonisation of the unknown.</p>

    <p>I am currently working on a new book, <em>Still Here</em>, structured as a topographical excavation of sites through modes of encounter — listening, reading, installing, diagnosing, gathering, letting go — with first-person interjections providing connective tissue across two decades of published work.</p>

    <p>I'm based in Sydney, Australia. Beyond research, I maintain a body-based practice through Pilates, yoga, cycling, and dance — and a long-standing interest in deep-time writing as a grounding counterweight to the accelerationist logics of the systems I study.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="affiliations">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Current positions</h2>
    <div class="affiliation">
      <div class="affiliation-role">Vice Chancellor's Senior Research Fellow</div>
      <div class="affiliation-org"><a href="https://www.rmit.edu.au/profiles/b/sarah-barns2">RMIT University</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="affiliation">
      <div class="affiliation-role">Founder &amp; Director</div>
      <div class="affiliation-org"><a href="https://studioesem.com">Studio ESEM</a> (est. 2011)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="affiliation">
      <div class="affiliation-role">Creator</div>
      <div class="affiliation-org"><a href="https://storybox.co">STORYBOX</a> &middot; <a href="https://civicinterplay.io">Civic Interplay</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Profiles</h2>
    <p class="profile-links">
      <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0087-7166">ORCID</a>
      <span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Sarah-Barns-4">ResearchGate</a>
      <span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=cnGxyWQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en">Google Scholar</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">My favourite personal work</h2>
    <div class="pub-item">
      <div class="pub-title"><a href="https://www.studioesem.com/projects/superorganism">Superorganism: Listening to the Anthropocene</a></div>
      <div class="pub-details">Creative Director &amp; Lead Sound Designer, 2022</div>
      <span class="pub-tag">Sound &amp; installation</span>
    </div>
    <p class="pub-more"><a href="/projects">All projects &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Awards</h2>
    {AWARDS.map(a => (
      <div class="honour">
        <span class="honour-year">{a.year}</span>
        <span class="honour-body">
          <span class="honour-name">{a.name}</span>
          {a.detail && <span class="honour-detail">{a.detail}</span>}
        </span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Fellowships</h2>
    {FELLOWSHIPS.map(a => (
      <div class="honour">
        <span class="honour-year">{a.year}</span>
        <span class="honour-body">
          <span class="honour-name">{a.name}</span>
          {a.detail && <span class="honour-detail">{a.detail}</span>}
        </span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Selected writing &amp; publications</h2>
    {selectedPubs.map(pub => (
      <div class="pub-item">
        <div class="pub-title">
          {pub.data.href
            ? <a href={pub.data.href} rel="noopener">{pub.data.title}</a>
            : pub.data.title}
        </div>
        <div class="pub-details">
          {/* Works with a yearLabel are unpublished — the venue already carries their status. */}
          {pub.data.venue}{pub.data.yearLabel ? '' : `, ${pub.data.year}`}
          {pub.data.citations && ` · ${pub.data.citations}+ citations`}
        </div>
        <span class="pub-tag">{pub.data.type}</span>
      </div>
    ))}
    <p class="pub-more"><a href="/research">Full research record &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Selected creative production</h2>
    <div class="pub-item">
      <div class="pub-title"><a href="https://www.studioesem.com/projects/wakulda">Wakulda: Weaving our Stories as One</a></div>
      <div class="pub-details">Studio ESEM &middot; Executive Producer</div>
      <span class="pub-tag">Production</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pub-item">
      <div class="pub-title"><a href="https://www.storybox.co/birds-of-australia">Birds of Australia</a></div>
      <div class="pub-details">STORYBOX &middot; Lead Curator, Researcher &amp; Program Lead (Studio ESEM / STORYBOX)</div>
      <span class="pub-tag">STORYBOX</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pub-item">
      <div class="pub-title"><a href="https://www.storybox.co/case-study-parramatta">STORYBOX Parramatta</a></div>
      <div class="pub-details">STORYBOX &middot; City of Parramatta</div>
      <span class="pub-tag">STORYBOX</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pub-item">
      <div class="pub-title"><a href="https://www.studioesem.com/projects/arrivals-and-departures">Arrivals and Departures: Memory Palaces at Barangaroo Headland</a></div>
      <div class="pub-details">Studio ESEM</div>
      <span class="pub-tag">Installation</span>
    </div>
    <p class="pub-more"><a href="/projects">All projects &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* About — elevated into the shared design language (scoped to this page) */
  .about-kicker {
    font-family: var(--body); font-style: italic; font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.96rem; color: var(--ember-ink);
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .about-tick { width: 1.7rem; height: 1px; background: var(--ember-ink); display: inline-block; flex-shrink: 0; opacity: 0.75; }
  .about-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .about-header .page-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--body); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.9vw, 1.25rem); color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 48ch;
  }
  /* Lead paragraph */
  .prose > p:first-of-type {
    font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 1.8vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text);
  }
  .prose > p:first-of-type strong { font-weight: 500; }
  /* Section headings in the display face */
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  /* Section headings sit in the same display face as the prose h2s above them,
     so the page reads as one hierarchy rather than two competing label styles. */
  .about-h2 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    line-height: 1.2; color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .affiliation-org a {
    color: var(--text-dim); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember-ink) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .affiliation-org a:hover { color: var(--text); text-decoration-color: var(--ember-ink); }
  .profile-links {
    font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-faint);
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.55rem; align-items: center;
  }
  .profile-links a {
    color: var(--ember-ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember-ink) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .profile-links a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--ember-ink); }
  .profile-links .sep { color: var(--text-faint); }
  .pub-title a {
    color: var(--text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember-ink) 38%, transparent);
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .pub-title a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--ember-ink); }
  /* Works still awaiting a URL — render as plain text, not a dead link */
  .pub-title a[data-needs-url] { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; pointer-events: none; }
  .honour {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr; gap: 0.4rem 1rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .honour-year {
    font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--text-faint); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .honour-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.12rem; }
  .honour-name { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.35; }
  .honour-detail { font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 300; color: var(--text-dim); }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .honour { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .pub-more { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .pub-more a { font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
</style>
